Karkov, whom the Weft call Kharkov and whose full name is Yuri Karkov, was a human [[Bestiary/Realmtouched#Duskwalker|Duskwalker]] of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] and a general of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]]. He was an older man with blue skin, and he wore the deep blue uniform of the First House. Many people who agreed with him followed him, and he had taken all three of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] bloods at once.

He raised two children as his wards, the elven woman called [[People/Althane/The Slipseer|the Slipseer]] and the orc [[People/Althane/Rampart|Rampart]] her brother, and kept them as his lieutenants. A locket in his desk holds their portraits as children. Both died before him. He held one of the few ultraviolet keycards to [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], the installation he ran with [[People/Althane/Natalia|Natalia]], and during the crisis there the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] pressed on his mind, trying to drag him down into slumber. He meant to fight it, and his wounds closed under a black silk like the one [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]] binds with.

He named [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] the mongrels who killed his people, broke the beacon and stole the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] the House kept, and their faces went out in flyers across Oresk to be hunted down and hanged in the streets.

The Weft killed him at RC3. [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]] shot him with the gun, which stripped his divinity from him, and [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] disintegrated the lower half of his body. Before the Weft could take the corpse, a portal opened and tendrils of the Deep dragged what was left through it.

The Deep remade him. What remains is a fungal body grown over the ruin of his own: blue skin under yellow, purple and green growth, three legs splayed radial from a torso cut off where the fungus took it, and little left of him in the mind. He is bent over a great fungus organ at the top of the [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|City of Yellow]], playing without pause. He does not play of his own accord: the tendrils that move him run from the hands of the Deep to his body and not to his head, so his head lolls as the body turns, and a voice near his own is forced through a throat the fungus has grown over.
